diff --git a/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-jinja-autoescape/design.md b/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-jinja-autoescape/design.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0728fa3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-jinja-autoescape/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+## Context
+
+`App.select_jinja_autoescape` enables Jinja autoescaping for a fixed set of
+standard filename suffixes and enables it for `None`.
+
+## Decision
+
+Normalize a non-`None` filename to lowercase immediately before evaluating the
+existing supported-suffix tuple.
+
+## Rationale
+
+This keeps the extension list and all existing fallback behavior unchanged
+while making the matching operation case-insensitive for the complete
+filename, including mixed-case suffixes.
+
+## Testing
+
+Test representative uppercase and mixed-case supported suffixes, and assert
+that an unsupported suffix remains disabled and `None` remains enabled.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-jinja-autoescape/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-jinja-autoescape/proposal.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c7c6c96
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-jinja-autoescape/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+## Why
+
+Flask's default Jinja autoescape selector only recognizes lowercase template
+suffixes. Templates such as `invoice.HTML` and `diagram.SvG` therefore render
+without autoescaping despite using otherwise supported extensions.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Recognize Flask's default autoescaped template extensions without regard to
+  filename case.
+- Preserve the existing behavior for unsupported filenames and unnamed
+  templates.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Affects the default `select_jinja_autoescape` behavior on Flask apps.
+- Adds regression coverage in the templating tests.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-jinja-autoescape/specs/jinja-autoescape/spec.md b/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-jinja-autoescape/specs/jinja-autoescape/spec.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..79da007
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/case-insensitive-jinja-autoescape/specs/jinja-autoescape/spec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Default autoescaping recognizes supported suffixes case-insensitively
+
+Flask's default Jinja autoescape selector SHALL enable autoescaping for
+template filenames ending in `.html`, `.htm`, `.xml`, `.xhtml`, or `.svg`,
+regardless of the case used in the filename suffix.
+
+#### Scenario: Uppercase supported suffix
+
+- **WHEN** a template filename ends in an uppercase supported suffix such as
+  `invoice.HTML`
+- **THEN** the default selector returns `True`
+
+#### Scenario: Mixed-case supported suffix
+
+- **WHEN** a template filename ends in a mixed-case supported suffix such as
+  `diagram.SvG`
+- **THEN** the default selector returns `True`
+
+### Requirement: Default autoescaping retains fallback behavior
+
+The selector SHALL continue to enable autoescaping for an unnamed template and
+continue to disable it for filenames whose suffix is not supported.
+
+#### Scenario: Unnamed template
+
+- **WHEN** the filename is `None`
+- **THEN** the default selector returns `True`
+
+#### Scenario: Unsupported suffix
+
+- **WHEN** a filename has an unsupported suffix
+- **THEN** the default selector returns `False`
